--select * from progressnotedetail where progressnoteid = 'f088b53a-6978-4591-bc86-0b63be2d573a';
update progressnotedetail 
set description = '<p><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Face to Face Contact Note</span></span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Child Name</span></span></strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;"> __</span></span><u><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Amia Batson</span></span></u><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">____________________________</span></span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Date/Time/Location </span></span></strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">___</span></span><u><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;"> November 15, 2024 3 p.m. @ Child''s Residence </span></span></u><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">___</span></span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Reason for visit:</span></span></strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;"> Monthly Visit/ Safety Plan</span></span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Other persons present for visit:</span></span></strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;"> Robin Butler (Foster Mother)</span></span></p><p><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">&nbsp;</span></span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Child Safety:</span></span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">During the home visit, Amia was observed to be physically and externally safe, free from any illnesses, incidents, or injuries and the same applied for baby Dominic. No concerns were observed or reported with the baby or Amia.</span></span></p><p></p><p><strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Physical and Mental Health of the Child:</span></span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Amia continues to have 40% hearing loss in her left ear and uses the device for listening/hearing assistance. Amia is currently up-to-date on all medical appointments. During this reporting period, Amia has had several urgent care visits for gynecology needs and sick visit medical appointments. Amia has received the proper medical care and testing and has had her medical needs met to maintain her health and well-being.
    &nbsp;</span></span></p><p><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Amia continues to receive Mental Health treatment through Turnaround; reports were received that Amia had missed a few appointments however, no further concerns or issues have been reported with the compliance of treatment. 
	</span></span></p><p></p><p><strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Progress of the child and the child''s concerns:</span></span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">During this monthly visit, a safety plan was put in place. At this present time, Amia’s foster mother, Ms. Butler has submitted her 30-day discharge notice for the removal of Amia and Dominic from her home. Ms. Butler has also officially asked to close her home to all current and future foster youth. During the discussion of the safety plan, it was discussed with Amia the consequences of not being compliant with the safety plan would mean that her child would be petitioned for shelter care and placed under the custody and guardianship of the Dorchester County Department of Social Services. The review of the safety plan explained the concerns of the safety of Amia as well as the safety and well-being of her son while he remains in her care. It was explained thoroughly to Amia the behaviors of concern to include not following directions and recommendations of the doctor for her medical treatment, missing curfew, and the allegations of resuming sex trafficking behaviors. The safety plan allowed for the supervision of the baby to primarily be in Ms. Butler’s care to detail that Amia can not leave the home unsupervised with the baby.
	</span></span></p><p></p><p><strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Child''s relationships or visits with parents, siblings, and other relatives:</span></span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">During this reporting period, reports were received that Amia continues to communicate with her mother via phone and FaceTime. Amia was originally scheduled to complete a weekend visit with her mother on November 22-25, 2024 to celebrate her birthday and spend time working towards reunification; however, the Department and Mrs. Bryan does not feel safe enough to allow Amia to stay overnight in Dorchester County at this time. &nbsp;</span></span></p><p></p><p><strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Child''s relationships with caregiver and staff:</span></span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">During this reporting period, Ms. Butler has felt as though her safety has been compromised. Ms. Butler has consistently been concerned with the changes in Amia’s behaviors. Ms. Butler feels unsafe due to Amia missing her assigned curfew, coming home in different vehicles than what she reports to Ms. Butler and having the vehicles drop her off down the road from her house instead of in her driveway, and also Ms. Butler has a concern for Amia’s hygiene and cleanliness due to the recent confidential medical diagnosis that Amia has received. Ms. Butler has informed the Department that she would like to close her home as a resource to any foster youth moving forward.</span></span></p><p></p><p><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">&nbsp;</span></span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Overall well-being of the child:</span></span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Amia has expressed that she will be in compliance with the safety plan as proof that she does not want to have her son, Dominic come into Shelter Care of the Department of Social Services. Amia has expressed that she does not want her or her son to be separated and states that if she had a choice in who cared for her son, she would like to have him placed with her mother. Amia reports that she will stay home from school or carry her baby to school with her to ensure that no one comes and takes him from her when she is not aware. 
 	&nbsp;</span></span></p><p><em><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">&nbsp;</span></span></em></p><p><strong><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">Additional Notes:</span></span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#3e4145;"><span style="background-color:#ffffff;">This caseworker and a family support worker arrived at the home of Amia’s current placement with Robin Butler and was greeted at the door by Ms. Butler, Amia, and Dominic. At the start of the meeting, Caseworker explained the reason the meeting was being held and presented the safety plan. Amia and Ms. Butler did not agree with the safety plan of Amia needing complete supervision of her baby. Ms. Butler felt restrained with those requests and did not want to be responsible for the baby full time. When Ms. Amanda (Clinical Coordinator of Pressley Ridge) joined the meeting, she was briefed on the conversation that had already taken place regarding the safety plan. Ms. Butler began to be upset when it was mentioned that notice was given that Amia had to be moved. During the meeting Amia was upset and at times said disrespectful things with rude remarks. Amia did not like the fact that Dominic could come into care if rules were not followed. She wanted to make sure and understand that placement was being identified for them both to be placed together. The safety plan that was agreed upon was that Amia could not leave the home unsupervised; if she was to leave the home unsupervised with Dominic or leave Dominic in the home alone, Dominic would come into care and custody of the Department of Social Services; Amia understood those rules and Ms. Butler provided her consent to be the supervisee of Amia and Dominic should Amia need to leave the home with the baby. Amia also wanted to know if she would still be able to celebrate her birthday with her mom, Marlene; Caseworker explained that at this time the overnight visit would be on pause and that caused Amia to become even more upset. Amia became more intensely frustrated and she started asking for her money back that she spent on clothes (dress), shoes, and hair that she had spent to celebrate her birthday as previously shown to the workers upon first arriving described as the shoes being clear and black in color with a very high heel and then showed us the dress online that was ordered which was a black evening gown. Amia stated that she and Mrs. Bryan would be going to the Hyatt for dinner; in the midst of being interrupted several times, Caseworker was trying to advise Amia that  the weekend visiting time with Mrs. Bryan could be revisited in the next coming days pending the outcome of how the weekend went and if compliance with the safety plan was followed. By the end of the visit/meeting, Amia understood and accepted the safety plan. She was aware that she had at least one interview lined up for the following week with the new potential placement, and that conversation would be revisited about spending time or an extended overnight stay with Mrs. Bryan. Mrs. Bryan participated via off and on phone calls from Amia’s phone as Mrs. Bryan would express that it was hard to hear or that she would need to hang up because she was in the middle of working. In the closing remarks of the meeting, Mrs. Bryan expressed concern that she did not want to see Dominic in foster care and that she would like to see Amia and Dominic back home with her; however, she would like for Amia’s behaviors to have been changed.</span></span></p><p><br></p>',
	updatedby = 'CDM-44063',
	updatedon =  now()
where progressnoteid = 'f088b53a-6978-4591-bc86-0b63be2d573a' and activeflag=1;